# idm's adaptive inertia sets pid0.j_mot (the loop's gain). Its gradient law
# speeds up with acc_cmd^2: in a fast id_mot run (10000 rad/s^2) it swung
# the estimate by 5x within milliseconds and the loop lost its torque
# (Yaskawa SGMAH, bench 2026-11-17, DEBUGNOTES "Identification: the motor
# can lose the track"). idm0.j_rate (default 1/s) limits its change to
# j_rate times itself per second. Simulated motor j 0.00003, started there:
# with j_rate 0 (as before) it ends at 0.00017; with the limit near
# 0.00006. The fit stays right either way.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
hv0.sim_j = 0.00003
hv0.sim_f = 0.02
debug_level 1
link id_mot
relink
start
debug_level 0
idm0.inertia = 0.00003
idm0.max_acc = 10000
idm0.max_vel = 94
fault0.cmd_error = 0
fault0.en = 0
run 0.5
fault0.en = 1
run 150
idm0.state
idm0.inertia
idm0.ls_j
idm0.ls_f
@expect idm0.state ~ 1.5 0.01
@expect idm0.inertia ~ 0.00005 60%
@expect idm0.ls_j ~ 0.00003 15%
@expect idm0.ls_f ~ 0.02 10%
